==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to construct a world where two AccessAttempts share the same AuditEntry — i.e., an audit entry is 'reused' or overwritten. The injection forces exactly that scenario, which the AppendOnly and FR_010_AuditImmutable assertions must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutable, AuditCompleteness
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)
      - AuditCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGating  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamGating.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows an AccessAttempt to be marked Permitted even when no active CareTeamMembership exists for the (clinician, patient) pair. The injection forces a permitted attempt with no matching active membership, which the OwnershipBasedAccess and FR_006_CareTeamGating assertions must catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_006_CareTeamGating, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_006_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ByteEquivalentResponse  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_ByteEquivalentResponse.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Denied attempt to return OkResponse instead of NotFoundResponse, leaking the existence of the patient to the caller. The injection forces exactly this leak, which NoInformationLeakage and FR_007_ByteEquivalentResponse must catch.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentResponse
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentResponse: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AlwaysOnAudit  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AlwaysOnAudit.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Permitted AccessAttempt to have no audit entry (auditEntry = none). The injection forces a permitted attempt with no associated AuditEntry, which AuditCompleteness and FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit, FR_013_NoRecordWithoutAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_NoRecordWithoutAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_IGOnlyAuditAccess  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_IGOnlyAuditAccess.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Doctor (or other clinical role) to invoke AuditSearch, violating the separation between clinical access and audit inspection. The injection forces exactly this privilege violation.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_011_IGOnlyAuditAccess
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_011_IGOnlyAuditAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttributionCorrectness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditAttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows an AuditEntry to record a different clinician than the one who performed the access, or a mismatched role snapshot. The injection forces misattribution by decoupling forClinician in the entry from the caller in the attempt.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_009_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_AuditFields: FAIL (expected)

